---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import ConvertFormat from '../../components/tools/ConvertFormat';
import RelatedTools from '../../components/layout/RelatedTools';
import { relatedTools } from '../../data/related-tools';
---

<ToolLayout
  title="Convert Image Format Free Online — JPG, PNG, WebP | Filekrush"
  description="Convert images between JPG, PNG, and WebP. Runs in your browser — no upload, no signup."
  canonical="/convert"
  heading="Convert Image Format"
  subheading="Switch between JPG, PNG, WebP, and HEIC — pick the right format for your use case. Free, private, instant."
>
  <ConvertFormat client:only="react" />

  <Fragment slot="content">
    <section class="prose prose-gray max-w-none">
      <div class="toc">
        <p>On this page</p>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="#which-format">Which format do I need?</a></li>
          <li><a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a></li>
          <li><a href="#comparison">Format comparison</a></li>
          <li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2 id="which-format">Which format do I need?</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Situation</th>
            <th>Convert to</th>
            <th>Why</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>iPhone photo won't upload to a website or form</td>
            <td><a href="/convert/heic-to-jpg/">HEIC to JPG</a></td>
            <td>HEIC isn't supported outside Apple devices — most portals require JPG.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Need transparency preserved from an iPhone screenshot</td>
            <td><a href="/convert/heic-to-png/">HEIC to PNG</a></td>
            <td>PNG keeps transparency; JPG doesn't.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Logo or graphic with a transparent background</td>
            <td><a href="/convert/jpg-to-png/">JPG to PNG</a></td>
            <td>Lossless, and supports transparency for overlays and graphics.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Speeding up a website</td>
            <td><a href="/convert/jpg-to-webp/">JPG to WebP</a> or <a href="/convert/png-to-webp/">PNG to WebP</a></td>
            <td>WebP is 25-30% smaller than JPG/PNG at similar quality — see the <a href="/compress/for-website/">web performance guide</a>.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>PNG file too large for email or a form</td>
            <td><a href="/convert/png-to-jpg/">PNG to JPG</a></td>
            <td>JPG compresses far more efficiently — trades transparency for a much smaller file.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>WebP image needs to open in an older tool</td>
            <td><a href="/convert/webp-to-jpg/">WebP to JPG</a> or <a href="/convert/webp-to-png/">WebP to PNG</a></td>
            <td>Universal formats that any editor, printer, or portal accepts.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 id="how-it-works">How it works</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Drop your image</strong> — supports JPG, PNG, WebP, and HEIC.</li>
        <li><strong>Pick a format</strong> — choose your output format and quality level.</li>
        <li><strong>Download</strong> — your converted image is ready instantly.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 id="comparison">Format comparison</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Format</th>
            <th>Best for</th>
            <th>Transparency</th>
            <th>Typical file size</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>JPG</td>
            <td>Photographs, social media, email</td>
            <td>No</td>
            <td>Smallest</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>PNG</td>
            <td>Logos, screenshots, graphics</td>
            <td>Yes</td>
            <td>Largest (lossless)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>WebP</td>
            <td>Modern websites</td>
            <td>Yes</td>
            <td>Smaller than both JPG and PNG</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>HEIC</td>
            <td>Default iPhone photo storage</td>
            <td>No</td>
            <td>Small, but poor compatibility outside Apple</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2 id="faq">FAQ</h2>

      <h3>Will converting formats lose quality?</h3>
      <p>Converting to a lossy format like JPG can introduce minor quality loss, especially if you convert back and forth repeatedly. Converting to a lossless format like PNG doesn't lose quality, but doesn't shrink the file much either. For a one-time conversion at a reasonable quality setting, the difference is invisible in most cases.</p>

      <h3>Why won't my HEIC photo open in some apps?</h3>
      <p>HEIC is Apple's default photo format since iOS 11, and it's not natively supported by most non-Apple software, older browsers, or many web forms. <a href="/convert/heic-to-jpg/">Converting to JPG</a> fixes compatibility everywhere.</p>

      <h3>Does converting to WebP hurt SEO?</h3>
      <p>No — the opposite. Smaller image files load faster, and page speed is a Google ranking factor. See the <a href="/compress/for-website/">web performance guide</a> for more on this.</p>

      <h3>Can I convert a PNG with transparency to JPG?</h3>
      <p>Yes, but JPG doesn't support transparency — any transparent areas will be filled with a solid background color (usually white) during conversion.</p>

      <h3>Is there a file size limit?</h3>
      <p>Filekrush handles files up to 50MB. Everything is processed locally in your browser, so larger files just take a little longer depending on your device.</p>
    </section>

    <RelatedTools title="Format conversion options" tools={relatedTools.convert} />
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
